        0 < physHead ≤ m_k ≤ physSum = 1/140     (∀ k ≥ 1),   `physSourceCondensate j = (1/200)(3/10)^j`.

    (`massGeneration`, `massTransmutation_ceiling`.)

# THE DECISIVE CHECK (maximally adversarial)

Does the flow GENERATE `μ_k > 0` constructively (⟹ the mass gap), or is the generation
the non-perturbative condensate = `singleStep` (the residual)?

**Both, split cleanly — the SAME irreducible core, in effective-action-flow form:**

  * The mass-term flow is CONSTRUCTIBLE (`massFlow`, `physMass`); the perturbative part
